From 4cba4dce63bfe891d959718be23b65b61e39ca17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:18:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Release 1.5: the game is heard when Unreal takes its window
 for one in the background (UnfocusedVolumeMultiplier 1.0)

HELD until the Mac confirms the cause of Brian's silent 1.5 (24 Nov).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhz35oCkUv94Xb2EwCjp
---
 unreal/TheaterCommand/Config/DefaultEngine.ini | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/unreal/TheaterCommand/Config/DefaultEngine.ini b/unreal/TheaterCommand/Config/DefaultEngine.ini
index 1547eac6..7a942c20 100644
--- a/unreal/TheaterCommand/Config/DefaultEngine.ini
+++ b/unreal/TheaterCommand/Config/DefaultEngine.ini
@@ -61,3 +61,10 @@ bAllowHighDPIInGameMode=True
 [/Script/Engine.AudioSettings]
 !QualityLevels=ClearArray
 +QualityLevels=(DisplayName=NSLOCTEXT("AudioSettings","Default","Default"),MaxChannels=128)
+
+; The game is heard whether or not Unreal thinks its window is the one in front. The engine's default (0) silences a
+; game it takes to be in the background, and a game started from the Play icon, which opens it from Terminal, can be
+; taken for one the whole time it is played: Brian heard nothing in 1.5 (24 Nov 2026) with the music playing in the log.
+; The sound director, 24 Nov 2026.
+[Audio]
+UnfocusedVolumeMultiplier=1.0
-- 
2.43.0

